  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-band set at Fitzgerald's in Berwyn, Illinois, on Friday, June 26, 2026 [1]. This concert is the four-hundred-and-sixtieth of four-hundred-and-seventeen archived shows for the band [2]. The recording, captured and transferred by ezralite23, runs for ninety minutes and includes twenty-three songs [1]. The set opened with a Cheap Trick cover, \"Dream Police,\" which is the only archived performance of that song [1]. Highlights include rare tracks like \"Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds\" and \"Dawn of Revelation\" [1]. Several songs were bustouts, including \"Alpha Omega,\" which had not been played in 937 days [1]. \"Letter From a Motel\" was a particularly significant bustout, absent from the setlist for 2,487 days [1]. Other bustouts included \"Source Decay\" and \"Black Pear Tree\" [1]. The band also performed \"Armies of the Lord,\" another rare entry with fourteen archived performances [1]. The main set concluded with \"Amy AKA Spent Gladiator 1\" and \"No Children\" [1]. For the encore, the band played \"See America Right\" and \"Up the Wolves\" [1]. The previous archived show was on May 30, 2026, at the 40 Watt Club [2]. This is the only available recording of the event [1].",
